## Complete User Flows

### Flow 1: New User Registration and First Login

```
1. User lands on homepage
   └─> Clicks "Sign Up"

2. Signup Page
   ├─> Fills form:
   │   - Email: user@example.com
   │   - Password: SecurePass123!
   │   - First Name: John
   │   - Last Name: Doe
   │   - Phone: +1234567890
   │   - Role: Patient
   └─> Clicks "Register"

3. Frontend Validation
   ├─> Email format check ✓
   ├─> Password strength check ✓
   └─> Required fields check ✓

4. API Call
   POST /api/auth/signup
   Body: { email, password, firstName, lastName, phoneNumber, roleID: 1 }

5. Backend Response
   ✅ { message: "Signup Successful" }

6. UI Feedback
   └─> Success toast: "Account created! Please login."

7. Redirect
   └─> Automatic redirect to /login

8. Login Page
   ├─> Enters credentials
   └─> Clicks "Login"

9. API Call
   POST /api/auth/login
   Body: { email, password }

10. Backend Response
    ✅ {
        success: true,
        token: "eyJhbGci...",
        expiresAt: "2024-01-01T12:00:00Z",
        user: { userId: 1, email, firstName, lastName, role: "Patient" }
      }

11. State Management
    ├─> Store token in localStorage
    ├─> Store user data in AuthContext
    └─> Set axios default header: Authorization: Bearer <token>

12. Redirect
    └─> Navigate to /dashboard

13. Dashboard Loads
    └─> Display personalized welcome message
```

### Flow 2: Creating and Managing Community Posts

```
1. User navigates to Community Page (/community)
   └─> Views existing posts

2. Create New Post
   └─> Clicks "Create Post" button

3. Create Post Modal Opens
   ├─> Fills form:
   │   - Title: "Managing Thalassemia Symptoms"
   │   - Content: "I've been experiencing..."
   │   - Optional: Upload 2 images
   └─> Clicks "Post"

4. Frontend Validation
   ├─> Title required ✓
   ├─> Content required ✓
   └─> Image size/format validation ✓

5. API Call
   POST /api/posts
   Headers: { Authorization: Bearer <token> }
   Body: {
     postTitle: "...",
     postContent: "...",
     mediaUrl: ["url1", "url2"]
   }

6. Backend Response
   ✅ {
       postId: 123,
       postTitle: "...",
       postContent: "...",
       userId: 1,
       creationDate: "2024-01-01T10:00:00Z",
       media: [...]
     }

7. UI Update
   ├─> Close modal
   ├─> Show success toast
   └─> Add new post to top of list (optimistic update)

8. View Post Detail
   └─> User clicks on their post

9. Post Detail Page
   ├─> Displays full post
   ├─> Shows all comments
   └─> User can:
       ├─> Edit post (if owner)
       ├─> Delete post (if owner)
       └─> Add comment

10. Edit Post
    └─> User clicks "Edit"

11. Edit Form Opens
    ├─> Pre-filled with current data
    ├─> User modifies content
    └─> Clicks "Save"

12. API Call
    PUT /api/posts/{id}
    Headers: { Authorization: Bearer <token> }
    Body: { postTitle: "...", postContent: "..." }

13. Backend Response
    ✅ Updated post data

14. UI Update
    └─> Post content updates in real-time
```

### Flow 3: AI Chatbot Interaction

```
1. User navigates to Chat Page (/chat)
   └─> Views chat sidebar with existing sessions

2. Create New Chat Session
   └─> Clicks "New Chat" button

3. API Call
   POST /api/chat/session
   Headers: { Authorization: Bearer <token> }
   Body: { sessionTitle: "Symptom Check - Jan 1" }

4. Backend Response
   ✅ {
       chatSessionId: 456,
       sessionTitle: "Symptom Check - Jan 1",
       userId: 1,
       creationDate: "2024-01-01T11:00:00Z"
     }

5. UI Update
   ├─> New session appears in sidebar
   └─> Chat window opens for new session

6. User Sends Message
   └─> Types: "What are common thalassemia symptoms?"
      └─> Clicks "Send"

7. Frontend Action
   ├─> Display user message in chat immediately
   └─> Show "AI is typing..." indicator

8. API Call
   POST /api/chat/session/456/message
   Headers: { Authorization: Bearer <token> }
   Body: { messageContent: "What are common thalassemia symptoms?" }

9. Backend Processing
   ├─> Saves user message to database
   ├─> Forwards to DeepSeek AI service
   ├─> Receives AI response
   └─> Saves AI response to database

10. Backend Response
    ✅ {
        userMessage: {
          messageId: 789,
          messageContent: "What are common thalassemia symptoms?",
          senderType: "User",
          timestamp: "2024-01-01T11:01:00Z"
        },
        aiResponse: {
          messageId: 790,
          messageContent: "Common thalassemia symptoms include...",
          senderType: "Bot",
          timestamp: "2024-01-01T11:01:05Z"
        }
      }

11. UI Update
    ├─> Remove "typing" indicator
    └─> Display AI response in chat

12. Conversation Continues
    └─> User can continue asking questions
        └─> Each message follows same flow (steps 6-11)

13. View Chat History
    └─> User clicks on previous session in sidebar

14. API Call
    GET /api/chat/history/{sessionId}
    Headers: { Authorization: Bearer <token> }

15. Backend Response
    ✅ {
        chatSessionId: 456,
        sessionTitle: "...",
        messages: [
          { messageId: 789, content: "...", senderType: "User", ... },
          { messageId: 790, content: "...", senderType: "Bot", ... },
          ...
        ]
      }

16. UI Update
    └─> Chat window displays all previous messages
```

### Flow 4: Admin Creating News Post

```
1. Admin logs in
   └─> Role verified as "Admin"

2. Admin navigates to News Management
   └─> Clicks "Create News Post"

3. Create News Form
   ├─> Fills:
   │   - Title: "New Treatment Breakthrough"
   │   - Content: "Researchers have discovered..."
   │   - Optional: Upload featured image
   └─> Clicks "Publish"

4. Frontend Validation
   ├─> Title required ✓
   ├─> Content required ✓
   └─> Admin role check ✓

5. API Call
   POST /api/news
   Headers: {
     Authorization: Bearer <admin_token>,
     Role: "Admin" (from token claims)
   }
   Body: {
     postTitle: "...",
     postContent: "...",
     mediaUrl: "image_url"
   }

6. Backend Authorization Check
   ├─> Verifies JWT token
   ├─> Extracts role from claims
   └─> Role === "Admin" ? Allow : Deny

7. Backend Response
   ✅ {
       newsPostId: 321,
       postTitle: "...",
       postContent: "...",
       publicationDate: "2024-01-01T12:00:00Z",
       userId: 1,
       media: [...]
     }

8. UI Update
   ├─> Success toast: "News post published!"
   └─> News post appears in public news feed

9. Regular Users See News
   └─> When they visit /news, new post appears at top
```

### Flow 5: Caregiver-Patient Association

```
1. Caregiver logs in
   └─> Role: "Caregiver"

2. Caregiver navigates to Profile
   └─> Clicks "Associate with Patient" tab

3. Association Form
   ├─> Enters Patient User ID: 5
   └─> Clicks "Associate"

4. Frontend Validation
   ├─> Patient ID must be different from Caregiver ID ✓
   └─> Patient ID must be numeric ✓

5. API Call
   POST /api/users/associate
   Headers: { Authorization: Bearer <token> }
   Body: {
     caregiverId: 3,
     patientId: 5
